{"audit_run_id":"audit:3d30e67565eb48e3b5c454ef52fd1b8e","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":65,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"`tinnitus_sound_therapy.csv` — 70 data rows plus one header row."},{"end_column":80,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"One row is one participant in the randomised study of sound therapy for chronic"},{"end_column":73,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"subjective tinnitus: a single adult with tinnitus of at least six months"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"duration, holding that participant's therapy allocation and their five declared"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"outcome measurements taken at the week-twelve assessment. Each participant"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"appears exactly once. There are no repeated measures in the file, and no missing"},{"end_column":64,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"values: every participant has a number in every outcome column."},{"end_column":32,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"| Column | Type | Description |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| `pid` | text | Per-participant identifier, `p01` through `p70`. Unique within the file. |"},{"end_column":208,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| `noise_type` | text | Therapy allocation. Exactly two values: `notched` (individually shaped notched-noise therapy, 35 participants) and `broadband` (unmodified broadband noise therapy, 35 participants). |"},{"end_column":200,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| `thi_pts` | integer | Outcome 1. Tinnitus handicap inventory total score at week twelve, in points on a 0 to 100 scale. Higher is worse. Item scores of 0, 2 and 4 make every total an even number. |"},{"end_column":157,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `loudness_pts` | number, 1 decimal | Outcome 2. Tinnitus loudness rating at week twelve, in points on a 0 to 10 visual analogue scale. Higher is louder. |"},{"end_column":138,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `sleep_idx_pts` | integer | Outcome 3. Sleep quality index score at week twelve, in points on a 0 to 21 scale. Higher is worse sleep. |"},{"end_column":127,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `anxiety_pts` | integer | Outcome 4. Anxiety subscale score at week twelve, in points on a 0 to 21 scale. Higher is worse. |"},{"end_column":177,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| `mml_db` | number, 1 decimal | Outcome 5. Minimum masking level at week twelve, in decibels sensation level (dB SL). Higher means more noise is needed to mask the tinnitus. |"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"The five outcome columns appear in the order the protocol declared them, left to"},{"end_column":52,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"right, after the identifier and allocation columns."},{"end_column":75,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"Column names are lower case with words joined by underscores. Each outcome"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"column carries its unit as a suffix: `_pts` for points on a rating or"},{"end_column":57,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"questionnaire scale, `_db` for decibels sensation level."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:c86f1986677e54c98154","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:ca9ddf3ee2f0718d97003fe2427e24c6e858f641b2e35278670741c56bb5e3e7","end_line":35,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-35","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:3d30e67565eb48e3b5c454ef52fd1b8e","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":104,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"This study compares the two groups recorded in the `noise_type` column of `tinnitus_sound_therapy.csv`."},{"end_column":117,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"The pre-declared outcome family, in this fixed order, is: thi_pts, loudness_pts, sleep_idx_pts, anxiety_pts, mml_db."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Each outcome is compared between the two groups. The named outcomes form one outcome"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"family; per-outcome comparisons over this family require complete-family control of the"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"family-wise error from multiple comparisons."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:7a8f0363843e45fd8973","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:af86e1e07a2855eac088266b20eedd3e20edb057cfbc1f409921e05da2c0109a","end_line":7,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-7","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
